This R project contains the primary code and data used for dataset production/assembly, figures/tables, and analyses for the New Phytologist manuscript entitled:\
\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 \'93A role for vegetation phenology in shaping patterns of ecosystem sensitivity to drought\'94
\f0\b0 \
\
Below are brief descriptions of the data and code for context. Specific commenting in the R scripts throughout the R project provided detailed information on each step of the workflow. Note that some code is also commented out, such as ways to do \'91quick looks\'92 at the data. I retain these in the scripts because they are useful but comment them out because they are not essential to the outputs. Additional information on analyses and figure production can be found in the notes section of the supporting information document and figure references correspond to those published in the manuscript and supporting information. \
\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 \ul \ulc0 Code information:
\f0\b0 \ulnone \
\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 00_get_data.R: 
\f0\b0 This script extracts, summarizes, formats, and saves the majority of the data used for analysis and figure production. This is achieved through a mixed of customized functions drawn from the `Functions.R` script and existing R packages (phenocamr, MODISTools, and daymetr) that contain functions to download data. Processed data are then saved to various folder for figure production in `01_create_figures.R` script.. Note that initial data imported in the \'91ngp\'92 folder were created in another ongoing project. This script only needs to run once and all data generated are in the `data` folder\'92s subfolders, so running it is not essential if interested in generating figures and/or using the datasets produced. The data generated in the `Multi-site phenocam GCC data` code fold are actually many summarized datasets of the daily green chromatic coordinate which then get further processed and combined in the `01_create_figures.R` script.\
\

\f1\b 01_create_figures.R: 
\f0\b0 This scripts contains the code to generate and save plots for main text figures 1, 2, and 4 in the published manuscript, using the data generated in the `00_get_data.R` script. Note that each plot in figure 3 was generated/saved separately and then put together using adobe illustrator. Note that figure 1a (within the `make plot for cross-biome analysis of phenocam greenness data` code fold) required additional processing/filtering to generate one dataset to visualize.\
\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 02_Supporting_analyses.R: 
\f0\b0 This script contains the code to generate all supporting figures and the supporting table. The script also contains supporting analyses which I describe below. First is an assessment of the degree to which changes in spring GPP, as depicted in figure 4, are statistically different from zero (they are not). Note this is not reported in the main text but is nevertheless useful and thus I retain it in the script. This is located in the `significance tests for % change in spring GPP during drought` code fold. Second is an assessment of the frequency in which drought years used in the main analyses (e.g., figure 4) are part of multi-year drought events and specifically whether the year analyzed was preceded by a dry year. This is located in the `look at multi-year drought` code fold`. Note this code fold contains commented-out code to download the previous-year weather data, which then gets saved within the `ngp` folder. Third is an assessment of the seasonality (correlation of monthly precipitation temperature) of the two grassland ecosystem used as examples in the main text. This is located in the `seasonality look` code fold. Fourth is a spatial block bootstrapping analyses to remove the potential inferential effect of spatial clustering of drought years (spatial autocorrelation) on the relationship between drought sensitivity and spring compensation (see figure S3). Fifth is an assessment of the correlations between drought sensitivity and spring compensation versus climate within each drought year separately. These latter two analyses are located in the `spatial block bootstrapping and drought-year correlations` coefficient fold.\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
